  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array arr[] of size N, the task is to count the number of array elements such that all the elements to its left are strictly smaller than it.\n\nNote: The first element of the array will be considered to be always satisfying the condition.\n\n\n\nExamples:\n\n\n\nInput:\n\narr[]={2,4,5,6}\n\nOutput:\n\n4\n\nExplanation :\n\nSince the array is in increasing order, all the array elements satisfy the condition.\n\nHence, the count of such elements is equal to the size of the array, i.e. equal to 4.\n\n\n\nInput: { 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3 }\n\nOutput: 1\n\nExplanation: The first array element is the only element satisfying the condition.",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= N <= 10^5"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "First line has the number of elements , and the line contains the set of integers delimited by space.",
    "outputFormat": "Print the count.",
    "notes": [],
